WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.710
Every answer has a story. With Paatam, we finally get to understand it.

2
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:20.070
I am a teacher, and Paatam reads my students' handwritten answer sheets, question by question. It suggests marks and feedback, but nothing is final until I check and approve it. Then the parent gets the update on WhatsApp.

3
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.790
And it all happens on one grading desk.

4
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:40.760
The overview shows what's been scanned, and what's waiting for my sign-off. Six AI agents do the heavy lifting, but the final step is always the teacher. Every suggested mark waits in my review queue.

5
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.770
In Classes, I can see which concepts a whole section is struggling with.

6
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:52.810
Student Analytics tracks every child's progress, exam after exam.

7
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.330
My answer keys and rubrics guide every mark it suggests.

8
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.930
The exam generator drafts question papers. I edit and approve them.

9
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:10.810
Our principal sees the whole school at a glance: the topics that aren't landing, and the students who need help.

10
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:17.340
Students see my approved feedback, and exactly what to practise next.

11
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.740
And parents get updates on WhatsApp, only after I approve them.

12
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:35.390
From the student, to the teacher, the coordinator, the principal, and the parent, everyone sees what they need. And every assessment makes the next lesson better.

13
00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:40.610
Paatam. Marks in minutes, and judgement stays human.
